The five reported moments are:

1. elaboration request;
2. expansion by the author;
3. system-generated measurement reflection;
4. attribution correction;
5. acknowledgment of origin.

The case is used to argue that:

- provenance can sometimes be restored in dialogue;
- framework terms can be reflected back with blurred attribution;
- human–machine exchange can generate candidate measures;
- source correction should be preserved as part of the record.

The nine measures are formally specified separately in #250.
